  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 462,
    "bookid": 34,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Localization",
    "headingPosition": 6,
    "headingid": 375,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 64724,
        "bookId": 34,
        "chapterId": 331,
        "headingId": 375,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Vagina and introitus vaginae (vulvar vestibule)</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-06-08T16:55:55"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 463,
    "bookid": 34,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Clinical features",
    "headingPosition": 7,
    "headingid": 376,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 64725,
        "bookId": 34,
        "chapterId": 331,
        "headingId": 376,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Thin atrophic squamous epithelium is susceptible to ascending infections. Patients report dryness and itchiness, pain with sexual intercourse, burning sensation with urination, and urge to urinate (atrophic vaginitis) {26125962}.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-06-08T16:55:55"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 464,
    "bookid": 34,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Epidemiology",
    "headingPosition": 8,
    "headingid": 377,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 64726,
        "bookId": 34,
        "chapterId": 331,
        "headingId": 377,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Atrophy is a ubiquitous process in prepuberty, as well as postpartum and after menopause. Atrophy also occurs in premenopausal woman during antiestrogenic treatment.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-06-08T16:55:55"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 465,
    "bookid": 34,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Etiology",
    "headingPosition": 9,
    "headingid": 378,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 64727,
        "bookId": 34,
        "chapterId": 331,
        "headingId": 378,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Atrophy of the vagina is caused by low levels of estrogens.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-06-08T16:55:55"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 466,
    "bookid": 34,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Pathogenesis",
    "headingPosition": 10,
    "headingid": 379,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 64728,
        "bookId": 34,
        "chapterId": 331,
        "headingId": 379,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Atrophy of the vagina results from a lack of estrogenic effects on vaginal epithelium and secretions.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-06-08T16:55:55"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 473,
    "bookid": 34,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Macroscopic appearance",
    "headingPosition": 11,
    "headingid": 386,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 64729,
        "bookId": 34,
        "chapterId": 331,
        "headingId": 386,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Not clinically relevant</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-06-08T16:55:55"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 467,
    "bookid": 34,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Histopathology",
    "headingPosition": 12,
    "headingid": 380,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 64730,
        "bookId": 34,
        "chapterId": 331,
        "headingId": 380,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>A lack of maturation of superficial cell layers (e.g. a lack of glycogen deposition) results in decreased thickness of squamous epithelium, which contains only basal and parabasal keratinocytes. The epithelium may be infiltrated by inflammatory cells and can be accompanied by considerable intraepithelial oedema (spongiosis), occasional mucosal haemorrhage, and epithelial desquamation (desquamative vaginitis). Regenerative and degenerative nuclear atypia can be significant, with perinuclear haloes (pseudokoilocytosis) in the more superficial layers. Thin atrophic epithelium may mimic thin immature or atrophic squamous intraepithelial lesions but lacks block-type p16 staining and mitotic activity. Atrophic epithelium shows no or only patchy p16 staining, as well as a low Ki-67 proliferation index (few cells in the lower third of the epithelium and no staining in the upper two&nbsp;thirds).</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-06-08T16:55:55"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 468,
    "bookid": 34,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Cytology",
    "headingPosition": 13,
    "headingid": 381,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 64731,
        "bookId": 34,
        "chapterId": 331,
        "headingId": 381,
        "headingText": "<p>See <a style=\"cursor:pointer\" href=\"/chaptercontent/34/286\" target=\"_blank\">section </a><em>Atrophy of the uterine cervix</em>.</p>",
        "timestamp": "2020-07-10T12:27:56"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 469,
    "bookid": 34,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Diagnostic molecular pathology",
    "headingPosition": 14,
    "headingid": 382,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 64732,
        "bookId": 34,
        "chapterId": 331,
        "headingId": 382,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Not clinically relevant</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-06-08T16:55:55"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 472,
    "bookid": 34,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Essential and desirable diagnostic criteria",
    "headingPosition": 15,
    "headingid": 385,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 64733,
        "bookId": 34,
        "chapterId": 331,
        "headingId": 385,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p><em>Essential:</em> thin, stratified epithelium without mitotic activity.</p>\r\n<p><em>Desirable:</em> immunohistochemical staining for p16 and/or Ki-67 may be helpful in cases with atypia.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-06-08T16:55:55"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 470,
    "bookid": 34,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Staging",
    "headingPosition": 16,
    "headingid": 383,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 64734,
        "bookId": 34,
        "chapterId": 331,
        "headingId": 383,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Not clinically relevant</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-06-08T16:55:55"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 471,
    "bookid": 34,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Prognosis and prediction",
    "headingPosition": 17,
    "headingid": 384,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 64735,
        "bookId": 34,
        "chapterId": 331,
        "headingId": 384,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Atrophy is a benign process. It can be improved by local or systemic hormone replacement {30897020}.</p>",
        "timestamp": "2020-06-08T16:55:55"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  }
